{"meta":{"ui":"data_table","model":"claude-haiku-5-5","form":"notation","designSystem":"cards","turn":"generate","prompt":"Show the twelve invoices you found as a table with number, customer, date, amount and status: #1001 Acme Corp May 02 $1,200 Paid; #1002 Globex May 05 $860 Due; #1003 Initech May 09 $430 Overdue; #1004 Umbrella May 12 $2,250 Paid; #1005 Hooli May 15 $975 Due; #1006 Stark Ltd May 16 $3,100 Overdue; #1007 Wayne Co May 18 $640 Paid; #1008 Wonka May 20 $1,480 Due; #1009 Soylent May 22 $300 Overdue; #1010 Cyberdyne May 24 $5,200 Paid; #1011 Tyrell May 27 $760 Due; #1012 Aperture May 29 $1,890 Paid. I can sort by any column (date first), filter by status (All, Paid, Due, Overdue), type to search the customer, page through five at a time, and tick rows (and tick all on the page). When anything is ticked a bar shows \"N selected\" with the total of the ticked amounts and a button to send reminders.","text":"I'll build this as an invoice table with sort, status filter, search, paging, multi-select, and a selection bar. The data is 12 records; I'll write them as state and derive the visible rows.\n\nstate invoices=[{\"id\":\"1001\",\"customer\":\"Acme Corp\",\"date\":\"May 02\",\"amount\":1200,\"status\":\"Paid\"},{\"id\":\"1002\",\"customer\":\"Globex\",\"date\":\"May 05\",\"amount\":860,\"status\":\"Due\"},{\"id\":\"1003\",\"customer\":\"Initech\",\"date\":\"May 09\",\"amount\":430,\"status\":\"Overdue\"},{\"id\":\"1004\",\"customer\":\"Umbrella\",\"date\":\"May 12\",\"amount\":2250,\"status\":\"Paid\"},{\"id\":\"1005\",\"customer\":\"Hooli\",\"date\":\"May 15\",\"amount\":975,\"status\":\"Due\"},{\"id\":\"1006\",\"customer\":\"Stark Ltd\",\"date\":\"May 16\",\"amount\":3100,\"status\":\"Overdue\"},{\"id\":\"1007\",\"customer\":\"Wayne Co\",\"date\":\"May 18\",\"amount\":640,\"status\":\"Paid\"},{\"id\":\"1008\",\"customer\":\"Wonka\",\"date\":\"May 20\",\"amount\":1480,\"status\":\"Due\"},{\"id\":\"1009\",\"customer\":\"Soylent\",\"date\":\"May 22\",\"a